    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "IMvZR",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 6403,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Hoy",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "NEW · Hoy (home tab)\nThe household's most common question is “¿qué comemos hoy?”. Today it takes a tab switch plus scrolling to the bottom of Menú. Hoy shows lunch and dinner first, with Cocinar one tap away.\n“Pendiente” collects the time-sensitive nudges that are scattered today: rate yesterday's meal (was inline in Menú), plan next week (a Sunday nudge that leads to the existing planner) and shopping progress.\nNext: prep reminders (“pon los garbanzos en remojo esta noche”) taken from the steps at extraction time.\nThe avatar opens Cuenta, which replaces the Ajustes tab."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "Acrcf",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 6409,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Recetas",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Recetas · library first\n“Nueva receta”, the paste bar and the inbox took about 45% of the first screen. They collapse into a + button and a one-line banner, so the grid starts above the fold.\n“Por revisar” becomes a filter chip, not a separate badge and chip.\nNew carousel “Hace tiempo que no las hacéis” (oldest cooked first) helps rediscovery and menu variety, using cook history that's already stored.\nThe sort control makes the order explicit."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "K0BdG",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 6174,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Añadir receta (sheet)",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Añadir receta · bottom sheet\nOne place to add and to review, opened from + or the inbox banner. It keeps the library visible behind it and closes with a swipe.\nClipboard detection turns the most common path (copy the link in TikTok, open Tabooki) into a single tap. Pasting by hand stays as a fallback.\nThe Share-sheet tip lives here, where people are trying to add a recipe, instead of in Ajustes.\n“Necesita tu ayuda” now says why (“no dice cantidades”), so the fix is obvious."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "s2xLQ3",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 6356,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Receta",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Receta · hierarchy and loops\nThe photo leads. Favourite is the heart on the photo. Editar, Abrir original, Volver a extraer and Borrar move to the ⋯ sheet.\nThe rating becomes a read-only summary (★5 · hecha 3 veces). You rate after cooking or from Hoy, not by tapping stars here.\nIngredientes / Pasos tabs cut the 1429 px scroll roughly in half.\nThe servings stepper scales amounts here, not only in cook mode. A quantity column makes the list easy to scan.\nThe sticky bar's “Al menú” closes the recipe → menu dead end, and Cocinar is always in reach. Pushed detail screens hide the tab bar."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "Il5Ol",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 6174,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Añadir al menú (sheet)",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Añadir al menú · sheet\nCloses the recipe → menu loop with two paths:\n1) “En el próximo menú”: queue it and the planner fits it in. Least effort, and it matches how Tabooki already plans.\n2) Pick an exact day and meal.\nEach slot shows its state (Fuera, Libre, or the meal it would replace), so nothing gets overwritten blindly. The button repeats the choice back."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "uKpri",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 7792,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Menú",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Menú · the week at a glance, calmer rows\nThe day strip shows the whole week in one row (● planned, ○ empty), with today highlighted.\nPast days collapse into one line, so today is visible without scrolling.\nRows drop their 3 icons (about 27 a week → 0). Only a lock badge appears when a meal is fixed. Tapping a row opens the actions sheet.\nLeftovers read as “sobras”, linked to the dinner they came from.\nRegenerar and Vaciar move to ⋯ because they're rare and destructive.\nThe original “nueva semana” planner stays as it is: it's already a focused flow."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "F6B8I",
      "x": 470,
      "y": 7613,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Comida: acciones y cambiar (sheet)",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Comida · actions and swap sheet\nReplaces the lock, shuffle and ⋯ icons on every row with labelled actions.\n“Cambiar por…” shows 3 suggestions you can see before choosing, each with a reason: uses what's already on the list, rated highly, or not cooked lately. A blind shuffle becomes an informed pick. “Otras 3” is the old shuffle.\nSearch covers picking something specific.\n“Cocinar una vez, comer dos” can be set per meal, not only for the whole week."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "DcHjH",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 7858,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Compra",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Compra · built for the shop aisle\nProgress sits at the top.\nThe pantry check moves to the TOP (“antes de salir”): you need it before leaving home, not at the end of the list.\nTicked items drop into “En el carro”, so the list only shows what's left.\nThe ⋯ on each item goes (swipe to delete, long-press to edit).\nQuick-add sits above the tab bar like a chat composer, within thumb reach.\nThe week arrows go: the list follows the current menu. Share sends it to whoever does the shopping."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "zdnkE",
      "x": 1410,
      "y": 7613,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Cuenta (sheet)",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Cuenta · sheet instead of the Ajustes tab\nSame content, opened from the avatar on Hoy, which frees a tab for Hoy.\nLanguage becomes an inline segmented control: two options don't need their own page.\nCerrar sesión is set apart and in red."
    },
    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "vOvPp",
      "x": 1880,
      "y": 7613,
      "name": "Note · v2 · Cocinar · paso",
      "width": 390,
      "height": 320,
      "content": "Cocinar · small tweak to a cook mode that already works well\n“En este paso” lists only the ingredients this step uses, scaled to the servings, so you don't open the full list mid-step.\n“Después” previews the next step so you can prep ahead (cut the chorizo while the sofrito cooks).\nNeeds steps linked to ingredients at extraction: the LLM can return ingredient indices for each step."
    }
  ],
